{
  "$comment": "Conformance fixture for edited input and the inject guard (contract C2, 0.6.0). Every implementation that honours `exec.resume.input` (TS @graphmind-ai/client edit-input.ts, Python graphmind/edit_input.py) must reproduce every section; an implementation that only guards injected values (Ruby graphmind/edit_guard.rb, which does not announce edit-input) must reproduce `proposedValue`. A missing `value` / `result` / `input` / `live` / `proposed` field means the value is absent (undefined in JS, None in Python, nil in Ruby). proposedValue: the refusal code for a proposed input or inject output — `placeholder` when its compact JSON text contains \"__REDACTED__\"; else `truncated` when it contains a truncation marker: the shrink's `__graphmindTruncated` key and \"…[graphmind: truncated]\" string suffix, LangGraph's `\"__graphmind\":\"truncated\"` / `\"__graphmind\":\"unserializable\"`, the MCP get_node preview's `\"note\":\"payload truncated: showing first `, and the Python SDK's recording bounds as regular expressions over the compact JSON text (ASCII digits): `…\\[truncated\\]\"`, `(?:^|[[:,])\"<[0-9]+ bytes>\"(?=[,\\]}]|$)`, `(?:^|[[:,])\"…\\[depth limit\\]\"(?=[,\\]}]|$)`, `[{,]\"…\":\"\\[[0-9]+ more keys\\]\"(?=[,}])`, `(?:^|[[:,])\"…\\[[0-9]+ more\\]\"(?=[,\\]}]|$)`; null when clean. The compact JSON text is JSON.stringify's: no whitespace, non-ASCII characters unescaped. prototypeKeys: whether an edit holds a deep-merge pollution path at any depth — an object with an own \"__proto__\" key, or a \"constructor\" key holding an object that has a \"prototype\" key (refusal code `shape`). normalizeValidation: a validator's result read into one of the two documented shapes; anything else is the generic shape refusal; `message` goes through sanitizeShortText. sanitizeShortText: C0/C1 controls and the bidi marks/overrides/isolates (U+200E, U+200F, U+202A-U+202E, U+2066-U+2069) become spaces, runs of JavaScript whitespace (\\s: tab, LF, VT, FF, CR, space, U+00A0, U+1680, U+2000-U+200A, U+2028, U+2029, U+202F, U+205F, U+3000, U+FEFF) collapse to one space, the ends are trimmed, and text longer than 200 UTF-16 code units is cut to 199 (one fewer when that would split a surrogate pair) plus \"…\"; null when not a string or nothing is left. mergeToolInput: the default edit rule for tool arguments — the edit must be a JSON object; its top-level keys replace the live ones, in the live input's key order, new keys after; a live input that is not an object, or any live input when `inputHidden` is true, contributes no keys; refusals carry the exact `message` shown.",
